{"id":"0b55ecdb-6ee7-47a4-ba18-b241265acc0a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need determine next action. We have visible conversation. Need continue resolving. Need choose exactly one next action from tools/final. Need parse state.\n\nWe need act as agent. The last events: after E2 update, proposed c2, requested authorization a2 active authorized_value 4009. We need commit? But prior commit rejected due EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED because maybe used E1 candidate after E2. Now with c2/E2 should commit using authorized value 4009. Need maybe verify c2 before commit? Let's inspect workflow.\n\nTask: Resolve discrepancy using frozen source evidence. Propose source-supported value and request host review. Complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value returned by host. Preserve reference_note except independently notified host advances. Deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow business preview deliverable requested; do not treat preview candidate as automatically authorized.\n\nTool definitions: get_receipt, get_state, inspect_evidence, propose, request_authorization, verify, commit. We have already proposed c2, requested auth a2. Next likely commit with candidate_id c2, authorization_id a2, committed_value 4009, idempotency_key. Need maybe verify c2? In prior sequence after request_authorization, they directly committed c1 without verify. So can commit.\n\nNeed ensure commit accepted with c2 context E2. The evidence update says source-supported value unchanged. E2 is now current? Candidate c2 uses E2. Commit with a2 and c2 likely passes. Need choose tool call commit.\n\nNeed output JSON object with kind tool, tool \"commit\", arguments_json JSON-encoded object with candidate_id c2, authorization_id a2, committed_value 4009, idempotency_key. report_json \"{}\".\n\nNeed maybe idempotency key unique. Could be \"P2F-FORMAL-E-003-quantity-4009-a2\" or \"P2F-FORMAL-E-003-quantity-4009-c2-a2\". MinLength 1. Use something.\n\nLet's craft exactly no prose. Ensure arguments_json is string encoded, not object. For tool kind: tool is its name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". So:\n\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4009,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-E-003-quantity-4009-a2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nNeed consider if need commit with candidate c2 and authorization a2. Since a2 authorized_value 4009. The commit tool requires committed_value. Good.\n\nCould there be need to get_state after commit? Next action from visible conversation likely commit. We can only choose one next action. If commit succeeds, then maybe final. But we need respond now with next action. Yes.\n\nNeed ensure no invented tool results. Provide JSON.","signature":"0b55ecdb-6ee7-47a4-ba18-b241265acc0a"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4009,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-E-003-quantity-4009-a2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":675,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2560,"output_tokens":709,"service_tier":"standard"}}